---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Medical Disclaimer | Chinese Gender Predictor - Important Notice"
  description="Read the official medical disclaimer for the Chinese Gender Predictor tool. This baby gender predictor is for entertainment only and is not scientifically proven. Always consult your doctor."
>
  <section class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">
    <div class="text-center space-y-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900">Medical Disclaimer</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-lg max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Important information about the limitations of our <a href="/" class="text-pink-600 hover:text-pink-500 underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors">free Chinese Gender Predictor</a> tool
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card-light-elevated rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4 border-l-4 border-l-amber-400">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-2xl" aria-hidden="true">&#9888;</span>
        Not a Medical Tool
      </h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
        The Chinese Gender Predictor is <strong class="text-gray-900">not a medical device or diagnostic tool</strong>. It is a traditional cultural chart used for entertainment and educational purposes only. The predictions generated by this tool have <strong class="text-gray-900">no scientific basis</strong> and should never be used for medical decision-making.
      </p>
    </div>

    <article class="space-y-10 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Not Scientifically Proven</h2>
        <p>
          The Chinese Gender Prediction Chart is based on traditional Chinese philosophy and the lunar calendar. There is <strong class="text-gray-900">no scientific evidence</strong> that this chart can predict the gender of a baby. Biological sex is determined by chromosomes at the moment of conception, and no calendar-based method can influence or predict this genetic event.
        </p>
        <p>
          Scientific studies have consistently shown that external factors such as the mother's age, the lunar month, or timing of intercourse do not significantly affect which sperm fertilizes the egg.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">For Entertainment Only</h2>
        <p>
          This calculator is designed purely for entertainment and educational purposes. It should be treated as a fun cultural exploration, not as a reliable indicator of baby gender. With a binary outcome (boy or girl), even random chance produces correct results approximately half the time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Many families enjoy using the chart as a lighthearted part of their pregnancy journey, comparing the prediction against the actual outcome. This is a wonderful way to engage with cultural traditions while maintaining realistic expectations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Consult Healthcare Professionals</h2>
        <p>
          For accurate information about your baby's gender, please consult a qualified healthcare provider. Modern medical methods for gender determination include:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-4">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-900">Ultrasound:</strong> Typically performed between 18 and 22 weeks of pregnancy</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-900">Cell-Free DNA Test:</strong> A blood test that can detect gender as early as 10 weeks</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-900">CVS or Amniocentesis:</strong> Diagnostic tests that can determine chromosomal sex</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Always discuss your options with your healthcare provider to choose the approach that is safe and appropriate for your situation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">No Liability</h2>
        <p>
          The creators and operators of this website accept no liability for decisions made based on the predictions generated by this tool. You are solely responsible for any choices you make regarding your pregnancy and healthcare.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <section class="card-light-elevated rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4 border-l-4 border-l-pink-400">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Remember</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-sm">
        Enjoy the tradition and cultural exploration, but always rely on your doctor and medical tests for accurate gender information. Your healthcare provider is the best source for reliable information about your pregnancy.
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
